<title>USA: TABLE - Multicare Cos Q2 net increases. [CORRECTED 15:34 GMT]</title>
<headline>TABLE - Multicare Cos Q2 net increases. [CORRECTED 15:34 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>HACKENSACK, N.J. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects the headline to show that the net increased, not decreased.)</p>
<p>				 Three months ended  Six months ended</p>
<p>					    June 30,	 June 30,</p>
<p>				    1996	 1997     1996     1997</p>
<p> Net revenues	    $ 131,889    179,164  251,946  347,956</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>  extraordinary item	 6,780     10,181   12,977   18,941</p>
<p>Extraordinary item - loss on</p>
<p>extinguishment of debt, -</p>
<p>  net of tax benefit	    --	   --    1,481	873</p>
<p> Net income		    6,780     10,181   11,496   18,068</p>
<p>Income per common share</p>
<p>assuming full dilution:</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>   extraordinary item	 0.24	 0.30     0.46     0.56</p>
<p> Net income		     0.24	 0.30     0.41     0.54</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>common shares outstanding</p>
<p>  assuming full dilution  32,565     36,656   32,511   36,652</p>
<p>		  (In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Multicare Cos Inc said on June 16 that it had signed a definitive agreement through which a company formed by Genesis Health Ventures Inc, Cypress Group LLC and Texas Pacific Group, will acquire Multicare.</p>
